  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Governance, Portfolio Management and Evaluation and Learning</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We are continuing work to embed Results Based Management in the organisation. Strides have been made but more investment is required. Evaluations to date have highlighted the need to strengthen MEL and increase capacity for project management, monitoring and reporting across the organisation. The project also supports accountability and knowledge management through reporting to our governing boards. The governance function will ensure the voice of member countries through High Commissioners is supported through convening meetings, providing papers and responding to members needs. The majority of Secretariat evaluations have underscored the need to strengthen MEL across the portfolio and review PMIS to ensure better integration with the other Secretariat system and increase user-friendliness. In relation to gender and youth mainstreaming evidence points towards the need to embed gender and youth equality further in the MEL and reporting system.</narrative>
  </description>
